  "description": "Our recipe for ziti takes a shortcut for faster prep. We toss soaked pasta with tomato sauce, ricotta, cream, and cubes of mozzarella cheese to form gooey, stretchy pockets.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 1 hr 50 min.\n\nOptional substitutions: ziti tubular pasta → penne tubular pasta or thick tubular pasta; homemade store-bought red sauce → high-quality store-bought red sauce; whole-milk homemade cheese → high-quality ricotta cheese\n\nNotes: Look for a ricotta cheese that contains nothing but milk, salt, and starter culture or acid. Avoid those with gums and stabilizers. Our favorite national store-bought brand is Calabro.",
